From b62bafa677fdb5deed06c6b0b06b15fffbcc79cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mattia D'Oronzo <doronzomattia26@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:16:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] power_supply: vendor property enum and sysfs tables

The HiBy charger, PMIC and fuel gauge modules (mp2731, axp2101, cw2015)
were built against a power_supply with the vendor's property list: 201
properties in a fixed order, with their sysfs names and the text tables
for the enumerated ones. The modules pass property numbers, so the enum
has to match theirs entry for entry, including the vendor additions such
as typec_power_role and usb_otg.
---
 drivers/power/power_supply_sysfs.c | 319 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 include/linux/power_supply.h       | 202 +++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 465 insertions(+), 56 deletions(-)

